      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The symptoms and presentations of gastroesophageal reflux disease are rather numerous. These include the typical symptoms, such as heartburn, regurgitation, water brash, or dysphagia. However, reflux may also be responsible for such symptoms as hoarseness, pulmonary aspiration, or asthma. It may also be an important cause of noncardiac chest pain. Thus, gastroesophageal reflux disease may be considered a disease with more than just \"esophageal\" symptoms."},
